{
  "$comment": "EXP-1270 (EXP-1259 D6): Getting started x4 = ONE block: a header row (the title `title`, the muted `{done} of {total}`, a `meter` px wide progress meter, trailing a Docs button (`docs.label`, concept `docs.icon`, opens `docs.url`)) over flat hairline-divided ROWS in `steps` order, one per visible step, in the list language (Danny 2026-10-12, the #EXP-1270 redesign: a vertical path replacing the row of square cards). The band is the group band every list wears; phones show Docs as an icon button. A DONE row: the step icon and title muted, a green check trailing; still clickable (do it again). The ONE NEXT row (first not done, `next`) is EXPANDED: the hover/glass-active fill with a hairline top and bottom, the icon + the title (medium) + a small `Next` label trailing (`nextLabel`), under the title ONE sentence of the step's `why` (13px muted) and ONE primary button labelled with its `cta`; the row and the button both run the step's target. LATER rows: plain, the foreground title, a quiet chevron trailing (muted at 45%); no numbers, no locks, no descriptions. Rows are at least `row.height` px (phones `row.heightPhone`), the step icon `row.iconSize`, horizontal padding `row.padding`, the expanded row `row.expandedPadding` vertically; the block is at most `maxWidth` px wide (the dialog is `maxWidth`), full width in the phone sheet; it scrolls vertically only, never sideways. A click runs the step's `target` (a step with `needsDevice` and no device opens `add-device` instead); targets: create-board = the create-board dialog, github = the GitHub connect step (web /integrations/github, desktop Settings > Repositories, phones open the web page), add-device = the ONE device-setup block, agent = the Agent page with the composer focused, invite = the invite dialog, add-server = the device-setup block on its server tab, mcp = the per-client MCP setup instructions in a dialog (web + IDE; done once an MCP grant or API key exists), widget = Settings > Widget. Visibility: `visibleWhen` names a permission (owner-only surfaces); `phones: false` steps never render on iOS/Android. Where it shows: on an EMPTY board (under the empty state), on the Agent home while the team has NO board (composer-home.json), and behind the sidebar entry `Getting started` (web + IDE rail; phones: the More tab row), which opens the same block in a centred dialog (phones: a bottom sheet); the web right sheet is gone. The block (and the entry) disappears once `complete`. Removed x4 with it: the lightbulb suggestion surfaces (action-suggestion concept rows), the action suggestion seeds (action-suggestions.ts + the natives) and the composer's suggestion rows. Model = pure `deriveGettingStarted(signals, permissions, platform)` (web components/getting-started/getting-started-model.ts, desktop getting_started.rs, iOS GettingStartedProgress.swift, Android GettingStartedModel.kt), every mirror replays `cases` (compare the WHOLE expected object).",
